 Responsibilities 
 ▪ Act as the responsible for the balance sheet and coordinate the analysis of balance sheet accounts; 
 ▪ Prepare balance sheet/profit and loss, budgeted balance sheet/ profit and loss and forecasted balance sheet/ profit and loss; 
 ▪ Produce monthly financial statements, balance sheets and cash flow statements; 
 ▪ Complete financial information for consolidation purposes; 
 ▪ Coordinate month ends and closing in SAP; 
 ▪ Analyze financial clauses of aircraft leases and make calculations in relation to new leases and amendments (IFRS 16); 
 ▪ Act as an internal consultant for all issues related to the consolidation and accounting of leases; 
 ▪ Analyze insurance and fixed assets; 
 ▪ Coordinate, communicate and schedule internal and external audits; 
 ▪ Respond to all requests from governmental authorities.
▪ Recognized professional designation (CPA); 
 ▪ Minimum of 5 years experience, open to candidates in public practice; 
 ▪ Excellent interpersonal and teamwork skills; 
 ▪ Strong interest in the use and maximization of SAP; 
